    <system:String x:Key="HelpHeading">Help</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpDescription">A quick guide to every screen in PosSystem -- read top to bottom, or jump to the section you need.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpGettingStartedTitle">Getting Started</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpGettingStartedBody">PosSystem has six screens, listed in the sidebar on the left: Dashboard, Checkout, Customers, Inventory, Settings, and this Help screen.

Switch between English and Arabic, and between light and dark themes, from Settings &#8594; Appearance -- the whole app updates immediately, no restart needed.

Some screens and actions are protected by an admin password (set in Settings &#8594; Admin Password) -- that's expected if you're not the owner or manager. Ask them to unlock it, or enter the password yourself if you have it.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpCheckoutTitle">Checkout -- Making a Sale</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpCheckoutBody">Tap products to add them to the cart on the right. Use the search box or category chips at the top to find a product quickly.

Adjust quantity with the +/- buttons on each cart line, or remove a line entirely with its delete icon.

Pick a customer from the dropdown above the cart if this sale should be tracked against their account (useful for debt/credit sales) -- leave it as Walk-in Customer for a normal cash sale.

Choose a payment method -- Cash, Card, or Pay Later -- then tap Complete Sale. Pay Later records the sale against the selected customer's balance instead of collecting payment now.

Tax and any discount are applied automatically based on Settings &#8594; Preferences.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpBillsTitle">Bills -- Viewing Receipt History and Processing Returns</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpBillsBody">Tap the Bills button above the customer dropdown in Checkout to open the list of past bills. This list shows every receipt's full history, including earlier versions of any bill that's been returned from.

Tap any bill to see every product on it, along with quantities, prices, and totals.

From inside a bill's CURRENT version you can return a single product, reduce a product's quantity by one unit at a time, or return the whole bill. None of these edit the receipt in place -- each one creates a NEW receipt with the same number plus a suffix (Bill #210 becomes #210-e1 after its first return, #210-e2 after a second, and so on), while the original stays untouched as history. Dashboard's revenue/profit numbers always reflect the current version only, so a return correctly comes back out of today's totals.

An earlier version of a receipt opens read-only, with a button to jump straight to its current version if you need to make another return.

This area is admin-gated -- returning a product or a whole bill changes real sales history, so it needs the admin password the same way Dashboard and Inventory's admin actions do.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpCustomersTitle">Customers -- Contacts and Debt</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpCustomersBody">Add a new customer with their name and phone number from the Customers screen. Tap a customer to open their detail page.

A customer's detail page shows their running balance (how much they owe from Pay Later sales) and their full purchase history, including -- for pharmacy stock, where applicable -- which batches and expiry dates were sold to them.

Record a payment against a customer's balance from their detail page to bring what they owe back down.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpInventoryTitle">Inventory -- Products and Categories</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpInventoryBody">Browse all products, grouped by category, with stock levels shown for each. Products running low (below the threshold set in Settings &#8594; Preferences) are highlighted so they're easy to spot.

Add, edit, or delete a product or category from this screen -- these actions are admin-gated, same reasoning as Bills: they change what Checkout sells and at what price, so they need the admin password.

When adding or editing a product, set its cost and selling price so Dashboard's profit numbers stay accurate.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpDashboardTitle">Dashboard -- Revenue and Reports</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpDashboardBody">Shows today's (or a chosen date range's) revenue, profit, transaction count, and outstanding customer debt, plus charts for top-selling items, payment split, revenue trend, and revenue by category.

Use the date range buttons or the From/To date pickers to look at a different period. Filter by payment method or category to narrow it further.

This screen is admin-gated by default -- revenue is business-sensitive information, so it's locked behind the admin password until someone enters it.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpSettingsTitle">Settings -- Language, Theme, Backups, and More</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpSettingsBody">Appearance: switch the app's language (English/Arabic) and theme (light/dark) instantly.

Preferences: set the tax rate and the low-stock threshold used across the app -- admin-gated.

Data &amp; Backup: see where the database file lives, back it up with one tap, and open the backups folder.

Export to Excel: download a spreadsheet of bills and sales for a chosen date range -- admin-gated.

Admin Password: set, change, or remove the password that protects Dashboard, Bills, and Inventory's admin actions. Leave both fields blank and save, or use the Remove Password button, to remove it entirely.

Access Control: choose which of those areas actually require the password -- e.g. keep Dashboard locked but leave Inventory open to any staff member. This section itself always requires the password, so it can't be used to switch off its own protection.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpNeedMoreTitle">Still Need Help?</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpNeedMoreBody">If this guide didn't answer your question, use the Contact Support card below to call, WhatsApp, or email us directly.</system:String>

</ResourceDictionary>
